  "question": {
    "text": "On a linear temperature scale $\\mathrm{Y}$, water freezes at $-160^{\\circ} \\mathrm{Y}$ and boils at $-50^{\\circ} \\mathrm{Y}$. On this $\\mathrm{Y}$ scale, a temperature of $340 \\mathrm{~K}$ would be read as : (water freezes at $273 \\mathrm{~K}$ and boils at $373 \\mathrm{~K}$ )",
